title: Global GUI variables
tags: GUI
kind: reference
audience: dev
aliases: global-variables clipboard metafolder.global
summary: One key-value store for the whole GUI, beside each workspace's own — what every workspace shares rather than one of them holds, the file clipboard first.

The [[workspace variables|Workspace variables]] are one store per workspace: what a
panel publishes there is told to the panels of that workspace only. Some state is
the GUI's, not a workspace's — the file clipboard is cut in one workspace and pasted
in another. It lives in the ''global GUI variables'': one store, held by the Rust side
like the workspace's (`GuiState`), so a script reads the same values and the
[[workspace-info panel]] shows them live, in a section of their own. They are not
saved: they last as long as the GUI.

!! The standard variables

|!Key |!Value |!Meaning |
|`clipboard` |`{paths, mode}` or `null` |the file clipboard: absolute paths, `mode` `copy` or `cut`; filled by <<cmd "clipboard:copy">> and <<cmd "clipboard:cut">>, read by <<cmd "clipboard:paste">>, emptied by <<cmd "clipboard:clear">> and by the paste of a cut, the sources having moved ([[Context menus]], [[file-manager panel]]) |

Like a workspace variable, anything else a panel, a command or a script writes is
kept under its own name — a panel's under its type (`file-manager:…`).

!! Reading and writing them

A panel or a [[user command|User commands]] goes through `metafolder.global`, which
is `metafolder.workspace` without a workspace: `get`, `set`, `setMany`, `all`, and
`onChange(key | '*', listener)`. Its calls belong to the
[[command transaction|Command transactions]] the command runs in, like the
workspace's: the command reads a snapshot of the global variables taken at its first
read of one, and its writes reach the store, with its writes to the workspaces, when
it ends or flushes.

`metafolder.global.current(key)` answers at once from the shell's copy — the value
last announced, outside any transaction. It is for what cannot wait for a call: a
right-click menu is built synchronously, and greys ''Paste'' out on an empty
clipboard with it.

A script reads them with <<cmd "GET /gui/vars/:key">> and <<cmd "GET /gui/vars">>
([[GUI scripting endpoints]]).

!! Why not a workspace variable

The clipboard was first a module variable of the panels' JavaScript: shared by every
workspace, as the panels run in one page ([[GUI design decisions]]), but seen by
nobody — no panel, no script, no `mf gui`. Making it a workspace variable would have
shown it, and cost the paste in another workspace. Neither was wanted, so the GUI
got a second store with the same rules.
